pve-gpu-manager (1.1.0-3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add transactional VF assignment, movement, and removal for stopped QEMU VMs
  * Bind assigned VFs with driver_override so autoprobe-disabled VFs work in PVE
  * Add guarded live PF switching between xe and vfio-pci with rollback
  * Auto-select the first GPU and add clickable VFIO and VF assignment cells

 -- PVE GPU Manager <pve-gpu@localhost>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 02:15:00 +0800

pve-gpu-manager (1.1.0-2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Safely untaint validated sysfs paths before writes under pvedaemon
  * Add a perl -T regression test for real and fake sysfs path boundaries

 -- PVE GPU Manager <pve-gpu@localhost>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 23:30:00 +0800

pve-gpu-manager (1.1.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add Arc Pro B50 and B60 support for the current xe SR-IOV debugfs ABI
  * Add explicit per-VF auto/custom resource profiles and live readback
  * Add transactional topology changes, consumer guards, and rollback
  * Add safe low scheduler default with gated experimental normal mode
  * Restore verified VF profiles and drivers before PVE guests start
  * Make PVE integration patches idempotent and upgrade-safe

 -- PVE GPU Manager <pve-gpu@localhost>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800

pve-gpu-manager (1.0.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release
  * Intel GPU discovery and identification (Flex, PVC, BMG)
  * Real-time telemetry (temperature, power, memory)
  * SR-IOV virtual function management (create, list, inspect, remove)
  * Boot persistence via systemd service
  * Proxmox web UI integration as native node tab
  * Compatible with PVE 8.x and 9.x

 -- PVE GPU Manager <pve-gpu@localhost>  Sat, 22 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
